    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d509">

                <pb facs="0587" n="507" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg507"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Reid.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-09-23"><hi rendition="#italic">September 23,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 6.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch of the 14th of July last,
                    with its inclosures, was duly received.</p>
                <p>The Department appreciates the dignity, efficiency and intelligent tact with
                    which you represented the President on the historic occasion of the proposed
                    coronation of King Edward VII.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
